# METIS .gitattributes — line-ending normalization (Issue #186 / Epic #183).
#
# Rationale: Windows clones must not corrupt shell-interpreted scripts via
# CRLF. `scripts/*.sh` and `.husky/*` hooks use `#!/usr/bin/env sh|bash`
# shebangs that break if checked out with CRLF. Cross-platform Node `.mjs`
# helpers (Issues #187/#188/#189) are likewise pinned to LF for byte-stable
# diffs across macOS/Linux/Windows. Existing LF files are unaffected; this
# only prevents future CRLF drift on Windows checkouts.

# Default: let Git decide text vs binary and normalize to LF in the repo,
# checking out native line endings per-platform unless overridden below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Shell-interpreted / LF-sensitive: MUST be LF on every platform ---------
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
.husky/*    text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.cjs       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.tsx       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.env       text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# --- Windows batch / PowerShell: keep CRLF (native to the interpreter) -------
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# --- Append-only history: auto-resolve by keeping both sides (Issue #1191) ---
# `CHANGELOG.md` is append-at-one-anchor, so two branches adding entries have
# nothing to merge and collide by construction. The union driver applies the
# resolution that was being done by hand — keep both sides.
#
# MEASURED LIMIT (2026-07-31): this fixes the LOCAL `git merge origin/main`
# only. GitHub does NOT apply .gitattributes merge drivers when computing PR
# mergeability: with this rule present on base AND head, a PR whose sole
# divergence was two appends to one anchor still reported CONFLICTING and the
# squash merge refused, identical to the control with no rule. The real fix is
# one fragment file per PR under `.changes/unreleased/` — see .changes/README.md.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# An agent-memory index is the same shape: every `code-issue` agent appends one
# `- [Title](file.md) — hook` pointer, so ANY two agents run in parallel collide
# here by construction — worktree isolation (#1147) separates their branches but
# not this one shared file. Measured 2026-08-06: a wave of four agents produced
# the conflict on the first two PRs to merge, and the resolution was a union both
# times, because both sides' pointers are wanted.
#
# The same MEASURED LIMIT above applies — this only auto-resolves the LOCAL
# `git merge origin/main`; `gh pr update-branch` still reports CONFLICTING and
# the fix is still to merge locally and push. Unlike CHANGELOG.md there is no
# fragment-file escape: the harness loads exactly one MEMORY.md per store, so
# this is mitigation, not elimination.
#
# ARCHIVE.md is deliberately included — it is a pointer list too, and retiring
# entries into it (#1206) is itself an append.
.claude/agent-memory/**/MEMORY.md merge=union
.claude/agent-memory/**/ARCHIVE.md merge=union

# --- Binary: never normalize, never diff as text ----------------------------
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.eot       binary
*.node      binary
*.wasm      binary
*.gguf      binary
*.onnx      binary
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff
